# Missing or skewed?  

Check two things before we create a recipe:  

1. Are there any missing values where we may need to include impute steps in our recipe, or remove variables or records?    
1. Are any variables so skewed that `step_normalise` alone might not be enough and transformations are needed?   



::: {#tbl-missing-skewed .cell tbl-cap='Check missing or skewed variables'}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Row per variable summary table, sorted by most skewed variable first
df_lsoa |>
  select(-LSOA21CD) |>
  summarise(
    across(
      everything(), 
      list(
        n_miss  = ~sum(is.na(.)),
        min     = ~min(., na.rm = TRUE),
        median  = ~median(., na.rm = TRUE),
        max     = ~max(., na.rm = TRUE),
        skew    = ~
          (mean(., na.rm = TRUE) - median(., na.rm = TRUE)) 
          / sd(., na.rm = TRUE)
      ), 
      .names = "{.col}|{.fn}"
    )
  ) |>
  pivot_longer(everything(), names_to = c("variable", "stat"), names_sep = "\\|") |>
  pivot_wider(names_from = stat, values_from = value) |>
  arrange(desc(abs(skew))) |> 
  my_gt() |>
  fmt_number(
    columns = c(min, median, max),
    decimals = 3,
    drop_trailing_zeros = TRUE
  ) |>
  fmt_number(
    columns = skew,
    decimals = 3
  )
```

